HakoSpace — Third-Party Open-Source Notices
============================================

This product ("HakoSpace", comprising the HakoSpace server binary, the bundled
web frontend, and the HakoSpace Desktop application "hako-desktop") includes
third-party open-source software. On Windows, the desktop application also
ships companion programs: the hakoHUD in-game overlay (section 5), two small
helper programs (section 6), and the hakoCap screen-capture engine with its
GStreamer runtime (section 7). Each component listed below is provided under
its own licence and remains the property of its respective authors.

As stated in the End User License Agreement (EULA §14, Third-Party Open-Source
Components), nothing in the EULA limits or overrides any right granted to you
under the licence of any of these components. In particular, for the components
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) — FFmpeg,
libuiohook, and the GStreamer runtime libraries shipped with the hakoCap
screen-capture engine (GStreamer, GLib, proxy-libintl and libnice) —
you have the rights the LGPL grants, including the right to reverse
engineer the component to the extent necessary to debug your own modifications
to it, and the right to run a modified version of the component by replacing it
within the software.

This file is a curated list of the principal components and every component
carrying a copyleft (LGPL) obligation. The direct-dependency manifests are:
  - desktop/package.json          (Electron desktop client)
  - frontend/package.json         (web frontend)
  - server/go.mod                 (server)
  - desktop/sidecar/go.mod        (screen-capture sidecar)
  - desktop/native/hako-audio-helper/Cargo.toml
                                  (Windows audio-capture helper, section 6)
  - daemon-v2/Cargo.toml of the hakoCap source tree
                                  (Windows screen-capture engine, section 7)
  - Cargo.toml, src-tauri/Cargo.toml and package.json of the hakoHUD source
    tree                          (Windows in-game overlay, section 5)
The exhaustive transitive dependency lists are the corresponding lockfiles
(package-lock.json for the npm trees, go.sum for the Go modules, Cargo.lock
for the Rust crates).

